      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If you are concerned about potential signals, physically covering the thermostat enclosure might block some external communication, but it likely won't block internal functions or sophisticated data transmission. A more robust approach is to isolate the devices by placing them on a dedicated, isolated Wi-Fi network, if your router supports it, often called a Guest Network. For advanced security, disabling the device's ability to communicate remotely altogether, if possible, is the most definitive way to prevent external data transmission.",
